## Torus with gap - inductance extraction test model
## Run: playback "S:/Radia/01_GitHub/examples/cubit/inductance_torus.jou"
##
## Includes STEP reimport (required for OCC seam fix + BEM)

reset

## Parameters
#{R = 0.1}
#{a = 0.01}
#{gap = 0.01}

## Create torus
create torus major radius {R} minor radius {a}

## Create cutting brick for gap
brick x {3*a} y {gap} z {3*a}
move Volume 2 x {R} y 0 z 0 include_merged

## Subtract to create gap
subtract volume 2 from volume 1

## STEP reimport (ACIS -> OCC seam fix, required for BEM)
export step "temp_torus.step" overwrite
reset
import step "temp_torus.step" heal

## Volume mesh (curve interval controls mesh density for BEM)
volume all scheme tetmesh
curve all interval 14
mesh volume all

## Allow elements in multiple blocks
set duplicate block elements on

## Source/Sink: the planar cut faces created by subtract
play "S:/Radia/01_GitHub/examples/cubit/inductance_torus_blocks.py"

## Conductor volume + full boundary
block 3 add volume 1
block 3 name "conductor"
block 4 add tri all
block 4 name "boundary"

## Save
save cub5 "S:/Radia/01_GitHub/examples/cubit/inductance_torus.cub5" overwrite
